acceptance_criteria: "The ordering-cycle finding reports the contradicting stored rows per cycle, not only the member item ids, so the evidence names what to remove; A holder that stores a legacy scalar blocked_by target together with a structured row asserting blocks on the same target is reported as its own finding code, separate from the cycle it causes; The remediation hint states the removal that breaks the cycle instead of advising that the finding be left as history debt; Validation or the mutation advisory refuses to introduce a scalar-and-row ordering contradiction on write, with a negative control proving the refusal fires; The eight surviving terminal cycles across 49 items are broken and the audit reports zero for the ordering-cycle code"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: "A cycle finding names the specific stored rows whose removal breaks it, so the remediation is a command and not an investigation"
value: "Every audit finding that reports a symptom instead of a cause converts into a research task, and research tasks do not get scheduled. This is why eight cycles have survived every hygiene wave."
impact: "Makes the last remaining legacy audit code executable, and generalizes to any future ordering contradiction rather than only the historical batch."
outcome: The finding reports the contradicting row pairs; a single documented removal per pair breaks every cycle; the same signature is detected on write so the class cannot recur silently.
why_now: "All eight surviving cycles were traced to one signature in a single scan this session, which the audit could have reported directly."
